@startuml US009_SD_3
title Deleting a logged item
autonumber
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant Frontend as UI
participant ":JWT Authentication Filter" as Auth
participant ":DailyLogController" as Ctrl
participant ":DailyLogApplicationService" as Svc
participant ":DailyLogRepository" as Repo
participant ":DailyLog" as Log
participant ":Meal" as Meal
participant ":NutrientScalingService" as Scaling
participant ":DailyLogMapper" as Mapper
participant ":UserProfileRepository" as Profiles


User -> UI : selects a logged item and requests deletion
UI -> Auth : DELETE /api/daily-log/today/items/{itemId} + bearer token
Auth -> Ctrl : authenticated userId and itemId
Ctrl -> Svc : deleteItem(userId, itemId)
Svc -> Repo : findByUserIdAndDate(userId, today)
Repo --> Svc : today's owned DailyLog with meals and items
Svc -> Log : removeMealItem(itemId)
Log -> Log : locate selected item within this aggregate
Log -> Meal : removeItem(item)
Meal --> Log : selected item removed
Log --> Svc : removed MealItem
Svc -> Repo : deleteRemovedItem(removedItem)
Repo --> Svc : explicit item deletion scheduled
Svc -> Log : isEmpty()
Log --> Svc : false
note over Log, Meal : Empty meals may remain while the daily log has other items.

note over Service: re-calculate nutrition summary
Svc -> Repo : save(log)
Repo --> Svc : saved DailyLog
Svc -> Mapper : toResponseDTO(savedLog, summary)
Mapper --> Svc : DailyLogResponseDTO with item identities and meal totals
Svc --> Ctrl : DailyLogResponseD
Ctrl --> UI : 200 OK + DailyLogResponseDTO
UI --> User : displays updated meals and daily nutrition

note over Auth, Service
If the item removed is the last one on the dailyLog, the
daily log should be deleted and return an empty daily log with zero intake.
end note
@enduml
